  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Liberia: Fighting Trafficking in Persons &#x2013; Phase III</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1) Targeted law enforcement and justice actors know the requirements of the Revised                Act to Ban Trafficking in Persons (TIP) (2021). 2) Targeted judicial officers and court staff have                knowledge and mechanisms required on judicial ethics and integrity. 3) TIP actors are aware of the                priorities and strategies outlined in the National Action Plan. 4) Law enforcement institutions and                civil society actors have the capacity to conduct awareness-raising campaigns on TIP.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Direct beneficiaries: Judicial Institute, Liberia Drug Enforcement Agency, Liberia                Immigration Service, Liberia National Police, Ministry of Labour, Ministry of Justice, Ministry of                Gender, Children and Social Protection, Ministry of Internal Affairs, National Anti-Trafficking Task                Force, National Police Training Academy, and civil society actors.Indirect beneficiaries: Liberian                population at large, particularly victims and groups at risk of trafficking in persons.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to combat trafficking in persons in all its forms in Liberia.</narrative>
  </description>
